## July 26 2026 — v0.5.3
astToBash

## July 26 2026 — v0.5.2
Rewrite bash parser -- better AST, fewer edge cases and poor parses.

## July 24 2026 — v0.5.1

### Nested parsing
- All per-parse mutable state (input string, rightmost failure, memo caches) now lives on a single `ParseState` object.
- New `runNested(parser, input, { basePosition })`: run an isolated parse inside another parse. Positions, spans, and error messages come out in the enclosing parse's coordinates.

### Error reporting
- `label` no longer erases failure records from strictly inside the labeled region — the deepest specific expectation surfaces instead of the outermost label's name. Tests asserting exact error text may need updating.
- New `committed(prefix, rest)`: once `prefix` matches, a failure in `rest` stops backtracking (`or` won't try later alternatives) and wins error reporting. `ParserFailure` gains optional `committed: true`; new helpers `committedFailure` / `isCommittedFailure`.

### Terminated scans
- New `repeatTill(chunk, terminator)`: repeat chunks until an unconsumed terminator — regions where the terminator is inert (strings, comments) can be skipped as chunks.
- New `matchedText(parser)` (raw consumed slice) and `many1TillOneOf(stops)` (`manyTillOneOf` that fails on zero consumption, for indexOf-fast bulk scans).

## July 24 2026 — v0.5.0
- Add `makeLexemes`
- Add bash parser

## June 3 2026 — v0.4.4
- Add `memo`, cache line table instead of rebuilding it on every call to buildLineTable.

## June 3 2026 — v0.4.0
- Remove backtracking support, add `peek` parser combinator for lookaheads.

## June 2 2026 — v0.3.1
- Fix: Markdown parser now parses markdown if headers don't have a blank line after them.

## May 28 2026 — v0.3.0
- New: `tarsec/parsers/markdown` subpath export — a CommonMark-ish markdown parser built entirely from Tarsec combinators, with ATX/setext headings, lists (incl. GFM `- [ ]` task items), tables, block quotes, autolinks (angled and bare-URL), inline HTML (open/close/self-closing tags and comments), HTML entity decoding, reference-style links / footnotes, frontmatter, and a nested-inline AST that round-trips constructs like ``**[link](u)**`` and ``*a `code` b*``.

## Apr 15 2026 — v0.2.2
- `quotedString` now allows backslash-escaping the inner quote — e.g. `"a \"b\" c"` parses as one quoted string of length 9.

## Apr 13 2026 — v0.2.1
- `quote` / `quotedString` accept backticks in addition to `'` and `"`, and the closing quote must match the opener (so a single-quoted string can freely contain `"` and backticks, etc.).

## Apr 2 2026 — v0.2.0
- Better parse-error reporting via rightmost-failure tracking — diagnostics surface the deepest failure across alternatives, with line/column info and a pretty rendered message.

## v0.0.19
- adds `captureCaptures`
